WEBVTT

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:45.660
Grandpa!

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.210
Oh, if it isn't Alice!

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.280
I'm glad that you seem well;

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.910
your complexion has a good color to it, too.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:58.330
But of course, it's the first time in 15 years that the Bats have won the division pennant.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:00.220
There's nothing that could make me feel bad now!

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.750
That's true.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.940
<i>Go! Bats!</i>

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:19.780
<i>Take them down! Go!</i>

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.950
<i>Go! Bats!</i>

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.820
<i>Take them down!</i>

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:30.070
<i>Go! Go! Bats!</i>

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:30.570
<i>Go! Go! Bats!</i>

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:31.670
<i>Go! Go! Bats!</i>

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.390
<i>Strike out!</i>

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.340
<i>They did it!</i>

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.510
<i>They did it! They won!</i>

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.650
<i>They won!</i>

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.560
<i>They did it, they did it!</i>

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.740
<i>They did it, they did it!</i>

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:05.660
<i>They did it! They won, Alice!</i>

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:15.450
Even the pipsqueak who I pulled into becoming a big Bats fan...

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.840
has become such a beautiful young woman.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:24.540
And now you've grown to lead the Bats to victory once again.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.960
I guess this means that I can retire with relief, huh?

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.310
You can't do that, Grandpa!

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:33.260
And it hasn't been decided that we'll win the championship yet either.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:35.980
After becoming number one we've had three consecutive losses!

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:39.760
And on top of that, we're going to {directly }face the second-ranked team today: the Rockets!

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.490
This time we have to win for sure in front of all the local Memphis fans!

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:46.730
Or else the players are going to get it!

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.400
That sounds scary.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:53.870
And also, even if we win, the playoffs will be right after it.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:57.200
You have to hurry and get well, Grandpa...

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.250
so we can work hard together!

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.090
Yeah, that's true.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.080
The ballpark is always filled with dreams.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:13.170
Show me a good dream, Alice.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.590
Yeah! Look forward to it!

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:23.610
You got it, everyone?

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:27.390
Today, everyone has to put their all into it and win the championship!

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:28.280
Yes, sir!

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.190
Do your best!

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.070
Go! Go! Bats!

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:36.290
Go! Bats!

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:51.040
This won't work.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:55.210
They've become really tense from the pressure to win.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:56.730
Pull yourselves together!

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:01.010
Strike out!

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:02.800
Hey! What are you doing?

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.530
Aren't your eyes open?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:10.900
Strike out!

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:12.360
Game over!

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:20.360
So once again, the game ended before my turn. {Literally "I didn't get an appearance again"}

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.840
Can't be helped; I guess I'll run home, then.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.280
Wait up, you guys!

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:28.160
Today's the fourth consecutive loss! Do you all know that?

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.430
I can't believe this!

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:34.390
Your shrill voice is {too }so loud{,} it hurts. {Kohn: I can agree with that, her voice can be quite shrill}

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:38.770
Don't you think the players know that best?

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.430
What are you getting so mad about?

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:53.440
This is unbelievable. Today they were Bad Bats. Disgusting.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:56.150
With victory right in front of their eyes, they play like that; it's-

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:57.730
Unreasonable!

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:01.040
If I find those players, they are going to get it!

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.500
We have to knock the soul of Memphis into them!

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.620
Stop that, you two.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:09.450
My grandchild is with us, please don't talk violently like that.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.920
It's Goro!

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:16.500
What!?

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.460
Hey, Shigeno!

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:21.980
Thanks for your good work!

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:27.680
You're the pitcher, Goro, right? We're always cheering you on!

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:28.270
N-Nice meeting you.

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:28.860
N-Nice meeting you.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:31.620
Hey, Goro!

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:34.480
The Bats couldn't win today either!

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.990
You're slacking off!

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:39.610
I am? But I wasn't even playing today.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.090
Shigeno.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:46.830
We're going to have a meeting to reflect on today's game.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.700
How about joining us?

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.200
Yeah, do so!

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.290
We'll treat you!

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:55.140
You should really eat a huge steak sometime{s}!

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:59.500
After all, you're always eating nothing but moist hamburgers, aren't you?

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:03.770
W-Well, I've still got training to do...

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:12.700
But still...

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:17.060
I guess sometimes a huge steak wouldn't hurt.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:19.750
Yay!

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.940
Goro plus meat!

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.780
We haven't introduced ourselves yet.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:27.960
I'm Charlie.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.880
And this is Greg and Marvin.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:32.760
This is Kathy.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:36.920
We were the first ones to set our eyes on you.

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:38.010
Do remember that.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:39.340
Yeah,

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:40.840
nice to meet you!

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:41.520
H-Huge!

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.960
H-Huge!

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:49.050
The pork ribs at this place are especially huge and delicious!

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:52.860
For real? Then I'll start eating!

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.100
Delicious!

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.020
And...

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:00.110
This is my grandson Peter!

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.750
Oh, it's Peter.

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:04.780
Hey, Peter.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:06.200
How old are you?

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:07.490
Seven!

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.030
The same as Shingo.

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:11.950
Is Shingo your girlfriend?

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:14.290
No, he's my little brother.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:17.210
And even younger, there's my sister Chiharu.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:20.960
I've got a girlfriend, you know...

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:22.380
But you don't have one, Goro, right?

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.720
Be quiet, you!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.260
Shigeno.

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:30.550
Do you know about the Hornets' Watts? {wattsu}

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:31.970
Yeah.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:33.240
That closer, right?

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:39.650
When he entered the Bats, he didn't stand out as a pitcher, but he threw a good ball.

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:42.940
And that's why we started to keep our eyes on him and cheer for him.

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:45.750
Since then, he's put on a conspicuous amount of strength,

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:48.170
and now he's the Hornets' guardian deity.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.530
Don't worry!

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:53.760
You'll be like that too!

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:55.290
Yeah, that's right!

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:58.250
We've never gone wrong with the guys we've set our eyes on!

00:08:58.250 --> 00:08:59.170
Exactly!

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:01.600
You'll go to the Majors and shine, no doubt{s}!

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:04.460
Yeah, that's how it's going to be!

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:06.460
But...

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:08.720
Before that, you've got to win tomorrow!

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:11.190
Or else, I'll kick you again!

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.110
Got it.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:27.110
And you seemed so full of energy this morning too...

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:29.580
Alice?

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:31.820
Papa! Mama!

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:33.800
How's grandpa? How is he?

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.010
Calm down first.

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:43.500
Now be calm and listen, Alice.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.880
The doctor said...

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:47.940
that my father's condition is quite bad.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:52.720
This is the third time he's collapsed, you know.

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:55.310
And it seems his body's resistance is gradually getting weaker.

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:57.310
This can't be...

00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:59.200
And that's the thing, Alice.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:03.410
We've been considering if we should all move to New York.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:07.000
W-Wait a minute! Why do you want to move to New York out of the blue!?

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:12.910
There are many better equipped hospitals there than here.

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:13.420
And also...

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:17.240
I know a doctor there that is a specialist on your grandfather's illness.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:19.950
He told me that he'd go out of his way to help. {Doing it as a special favor to his friend.}

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:25.590
B-But if we move, what will happen to the Bats!?

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:28.800
About that...

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:32.940
{With}Under these circumstances, I think my father should stop managing the baseball team.

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:36.180
As my father is right now...

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:39.950
I want him to think about his health as his top priority.

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:41.980
And also...

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:43.940
We haven't said anything to you, but...

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:46.360
we've been looking for a new caretaker for the baseball team.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:47.900
A caretaker?

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:49.400
And then last week...

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.570
A businessman in Nashville... {nashubiru}

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:55.660
accepted to become the new owner of the team.

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:57.330
Nashville...

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:58.760
So far away...

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:02.540
Even {if}though it's far, it's still in the {same }Tennessee state{, though}.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:05.000
But it isn't Memphis!

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:06.350
Alice...

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:09.300
What about the Memphis{'} fans then!?

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.420
They've all cheered for us since a long time ago...

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.430
because we are their local baseball team!

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:14.520
Alice!

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:16.360
It's a necessary thing to do!

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.010
Please understand.

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:24.820
I don't understand.

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:27.650
The Memphis Bats are...

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:29.910
what grandpa lives for, aren't they?

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:31.190
Myself also...

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.000
and all the fans too.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:38.170
The Bats...

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:41.130
have got to be the Memphis Bats!

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:50.340
Okay.

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:54.090
I thought I would ask you to convince my father, but...

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.510
I will talk to him myself.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:03.700
This is a free fansub.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:03.700
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:17.990
<i>I'm going now.</i>

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:20.030
<i>Do your best as well, grandpa.</i>

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:36.880
Today the Bats will win the division pennant for sure!

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:38.640
Oh yeah!

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:40.350
I'm looking forward to it!

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:46.230
<i>It's true that...</i>

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:50.810
<i>it might be best for grandpa's health if we move to New York...</i>

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:52.830
<i>But...</i>

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:57.150
<i>do the Bats really have to become separated from Memphis {for}because of that?</i>

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:05.750
Yo!

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:09.720
Shigeno-kun!

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:12.790
What's with that gloomy face?

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:14.550
Don't worry.

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:18.060
Today we'll win the {district}division pennant for sure.

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:21.480
You're right.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:25.070
What did you say, you bastard!?

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:26.990
Try to say that again!

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:29.520
I'll say it as many times as you want.

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:33.150
The Rockets will win today too and make a comeback victory in the league.

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:37.170
It's 15 years too early for the clumsy Bats to be able to win.

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:40.740
Hey, you! I won't forgive you for speaking badly of the Bats!

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:41.700
That's right!

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:44.090
As honor-filled Bats fans, we won't stand for it!

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.220
Stop it, Peter.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.170
Hey, hey, you guys!

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:57.100
What are you doing?

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:59.270
Stop with this nonsense!

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:01.820
Shigeno-kun!

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.050
Shigeno!

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:07.100
Hey, Shigeno!

00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:07.770
Goro!

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:09.160
Are you all right, dear?

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:11.770
Shigeno, isn't that...

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:12.870
That closer...

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.940
Are you really all right?

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:17.280
Yeah, I only fell down.

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:19.490
But you didn't hurt your hand, did you?

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:21.400
Show it to me.

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:24.280
It's all right, I'm telling you. You're all exaggerating.

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:25.670
Don't say such a stupid thing!

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:28.040
W-What is it? Why are you so angry, Gramps?

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:30.710
W-What is it? Why are you so angry, Gramps?

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:35.720
Shigeno.

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:39.630
It's not only your dreams...

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:43.310
The dreams of all of us fans are counting on this left arm!

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:48.260
<i>Dreams...</i>

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:49.560
That's right!

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:52.350
Yeah. It's only natural that we worry.

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:53.810
That's right, Goro.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:56.900
Yeah, that's right. {Just lots of agreeing.}

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:00.820
Thank you.

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:02.150
Leave it to me!

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:04.070
We're counting on you!

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:07.910
Geez, <i>this</i> part is where it hurts, you know...

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:22.720
Hello?

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:23.350
Mama?

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:26.820
I've got a request.

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:38.080
Over here!

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:41.690
Alice, why did you call us at such a time?

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:43.950
Your father and I must stay with my father, or...

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:45.040
Yeah.

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:47.070
Please...

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:53.300
Please, I want you to watch the Memphis Bats' game closely, in this stadium, before the end! {Or "one more time", before they decide on the moving, I believe}

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:57.750
Grandpa...

00:15:57.750 --> 00:15:59.380
He always said...

00:16:01.590 --> 00:16:05.090
"The ballpark is always filled with dreams."

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:12.990
I want to burn those dreams into {Papa and Mama's}your eyes before the end!

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:15.060
Alice...

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:17.350
You punks!

00:16:17.730 --> 00:16:20.770
How many times will you make me say the same thing...

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:22.250
until you're satisfied!?

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:26.150
Get it?

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:29.840
Today is the day that we, by all costs, will absolutely win!

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.300
Yeah!

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.200
Go! Go! Bats!

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:32.740
Go! Go! Bats!

00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:33.970
Go! Go! Bats!

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:43.430
Play ball!

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:30.190
Well, well, the Memphis Bats...

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:32.050
for the first time in 15 years...

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:35.530
are finally reaching their dream of winning the division pennant!

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:36.640
And...

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:39.600
entering the stage in the ninth inning is of course...

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.280
the suppressor, the trump card:

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:46.150
Goro Shigeno!

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.050
Shigeno!

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:12.760
Go, Goro!

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:14.470
We're counting on you, Shigeno!

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:16.240
All our dreams...

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:19.280
Make them come true!

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:27.280
<i>Please, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:29.190
<i>Make our dreams come true.</i>

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.330
<i>Let's do this!</i>

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:12.750
Strike two!

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:21.410
<i>Far from the outside, I got it.</i>

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:27.520
Strike out!

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:36.550
Strike out!

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:41.310
<i>This guy...</i>

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:44.890
Just one more...

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:46.030
Goro...

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.780
Strike two!

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:08.130
<i>Half a ball outside the strike zone. {Almost a strike, but just outside}</i>

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:11.380
<i>You can do it as you are right now.</i>

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:38.110
Strike out!

00:20:38.110 --> 00:20:39.880
Game over!

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:42.760
You did it!

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:44.380
Yay!

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:49.880
Don't dodge!

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:51.970
We did it! We did it!

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:53.960
Let me in too!

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:59.430
They did it! They won!

00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:00.860
For the first time in 15 years...

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:02.100
the Memphis Bats have won...

00:21:02.100 --> 00:21:05.180
the Eastern Division Pennant!

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:14.730
They did it!

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:18.420
You won! Goro!

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:38.020
<i>Isn't it wonderful, Mary?</i>

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:41.270
<i>The ballpark is always filled with dreams.</i>

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:42.640
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:53.020
Hello, Gordon?

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:54.190
Yes.

00:21:55.110 --> 00:21:55.860
Yes.

00:21:57.940 --> 00:21:59.490
I see.

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:00.630
Thank you!

00:22:02.950 --> 00:22:09.250
He said that father apparently heard the radio announcement...

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:10.890
and woke up...

00:22:12.210 --> 00:22:13.880
I see!

00:22:13.880 --> 00:22:16.340
The dreams of my father and Alice...

00:22:16.340 --> 00:22:19.130
and of all the people gathered here, are in this place. {This city}

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:22.800
And the players who grant their dreams are here.

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:25.610
That hasn't changed.

00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:29.910
We'll have to reconsider moving to New York, don't you agree?

00:22:31.060 --> 00:22:32.310
That's right.

00:24:10.920 --> 00:24:13.680
As the Bats have finally fulfilled their wish to win the division pennant...

00:24:13.680 --> 00:24:17.390
We'll use the spirit we've accumulated and dominate in the playoffs as well!

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:18.210
What?

00:24:18.210 --> 00:24:20.040
The boss has called for me?

00:24:20.040 --> 00:24:21.810
Have I done something wrong?

00:24:22.630 --> 00:24:23.350
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.840 --> 00:24:25.060
Decision.

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:27.510
Run towards the stage of your dreams!
